From 6866652ba09a4ca179a6da9a943832f6d3579e61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 05:54:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_typeck: expand an associated type whose impl has
 where-clause-only params

tower 0.5.3 util/boxed_clone.rs:72 (ast-grep 0.45.3), after 0162:

    let inner = inner.map_future(|f| Box::pin(f) as _);
    BoxCloneService(Box::new(inner))   // Box<dyn CloneService<T, .., Future = BoxFuture<..>> + Send>

    Spare rule - _Cast {Pin<Box<<S as Service<T>>::Future>>} -> _

The same MapFuture shape as 0162, through `trait CloneService<R>:
Service<R>` and `impl<R, T> CloneService<R> for T where T: Service<R>
+ ..`. That blanket impl has no `Future`, so check_associated falls
back to expanding `<MapFuture<S, closure> as Service<T>>::Future` in
expand_associated_types. That function also refused any impl with
placeholder params ("Placeholder parameters present in impl, can't
expand"), although `type Future = Fut` names only the closure's
return type, and `T`/`E` sit in the where-clause.

It now refuses only when the expanded type itself names a placeholder,
matching 0162. The impl's bounds are checked where the impl was
selected, as for any fuzzy single impl.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
index b364c678..40af0b5e 100644
--- a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
@@ -3009,8 +3009,14 @@ void TraitResolution::expand_associated_types_inplace__UfcsKnown(const Span& sp,
                 //ERROR(sp, E0000, "Couldn't find assocated type " << pe.item << " in impl of " << pe.trait << " for " << pe.type);
             }
 
-            // Try again later?
-            if( best_impl.has_magic_params() ) {
+            // Try again later? Only if the value names a placeholder: impl params that appear only in where-clauses
+            // don't change it (as in `check_associated`)
+            // - tower 0.5.3 util/boxed_clone.rs:72: `<MapFuture<S, closure> as CloneService<T>>::Future` goes through
+            //   the blanket impl to MapFuture's `Service` impl, `type Future = Fut` with `T`/`E` only in
+            //   `Fut: Future<Output = Result<T, E>>` -> never expanded -> "Spare rule - _Cast {..} -> _"
+            if( best_impl.has_magic_params() && visit_ty_with(ty, [](const ::HIR::TypeRef& t) {
+                    return t.data().is_Generic() && t.data().as_Generic().is_placeholder();
+                    }) ) {
                 DEBUG("- Placeholder parameters present in impl, can't expand");
                 return ;
             }
